            "uri": "https://github.com/urllib3/urllib3/pull/5161",
            "text": "Following a 303 redirect, urllib3 switches the method to `GET` and drops the request body per RFC 9110, Section 15.4.4 \u2014 but the state that *describes* that body survives the switch. Two things go wrong as a result.\r\n\r\n### 1. The redirected",
            "original_chars": 4631,
            "revision": "a37bc93b65d6bcf00d3dc43d966bab6bd130ecd8",
            "revision_basis": "indexed_checkout_not_source_revision",
            "snapshot_at": "2026-10-15T15:39:29.758191+00:00",
            "work_uid": "github.com/urllib3/urllib3:pr:5161",
            "work_type": "PR",
            "work_status": "merged",
            "status_basis": "github_api_snapshot",
            "merged_at": "2026-09-08T19:59:50Z",
            "retrieval": "direct_source_link",
            "association": "file_level_historical",
            "symbol_constraint": false,
            "truncated": true,
            "scope": "org",
            "repo_id": "github.com/urllib3/urllib3",
            "trust_status": "untrusted_evidence",
            "binding": false,
            "evidence_confidence": "recorded_source",
            "example_display_truncated": true
          },
          {
            "source_uid": "github.com/urllib3/urllib3:pr:5242:source",
            "uri": "https://github.com/urllib3/urllib3/pull/5242",
            "text": "Fixes #5181.\r\n\r\n## The bug\r\n\r\n`HTTPConnectionPool.urlopen` records where a file-like body starts, so that it can rewind the body before resending it on a redirect. `PoolManager.urlopen` turns that machinery off (`kw[\"redirect\"] = False`) an",
            "original_chars": 3548,
            "revision": "a37bc93b65d6bcf00d3dc43d966bab6bd130ecd8",
            "revision_basis": "indexed_checkout_not_source_revision",
            "snapshot_at": "2026-10-15T15:39:29.758191+00:00",
            "work_uid": "github.com/urllib3/urllib3:pr:5242",
